<node id="Signal S-201">
  <data key="d0">Signal S-201</data>
  <data key="d1">signal</data>
  <data key="d2">Signal S-201 is a temperature measurement signal that monitors the thermal conditions of a process tank. This entity provides crucial information on the tank's temperature, which is essential for maintaining optimal processes and ensuring safe operation.

The description suggests that Signal S-201 measures the temperature within the process tank, consistently providing readings to inform subsequent steps in the manufacturing or processing sequence. Furthermore, it seems that this signal is involved in controlling V-101 and C-900, highlighting its significance in regulating the surrounding equipment or systems.

In addition to temperature monitoring, some descriptions also mention Signal S-201 being related to flow level measurements from Tank T-501. Although the exact nature of this connection is unclear, it implies that Signal S-201 might be part of a more comprehensive sensing system that tracks flow rates and tank levels.

It's essential to note that all descriptions consistently portray Signal S-201 as a temperature measurement signal focused on process tank monitoring. The presence of additional context or connections with other sensors (like Tank T-501) further underscores the importance of this signal in maintaining a safe and efficient operation.</data>
